prompt:
Public specification:
Given the state-assigned table shown below, implement the logic functions Y[0] and z.
// Present state y[2:0] | Next state Y[2:0] x=0, Next state Y[2:0] x=1 | Output z
// 000 | 000, 001 | 0
// 001 | 001, 100 | 0
// 010 | 010, 001 | 0
// 011 | 001, 010 | 1
// 100 | 011, 100 | 1


Input widths {'x': 1, 'y': 3}; output widths {'Y0': 1, 'z': 1}. Clock clk; sample after the posedge edge has settled. Each row's values are driven before the sampled edge. Optional mid input changes occur AFTER sampling, before the other edge, and are carried to the start of the next row. Protocol seed 20261123.
Write a compact JSON Veri-Sure B.1 contract with module_name (top_module), io list with name, dir, width, description, clocking {clock:{name,edge} or null, reset:{name,active,kind} or null}, timing {outputs:{name:{latency_cycles:nonnegative integer}}}, functional_summary {overview, rules}. Public interface must match (include the clock in io).

response:
```json
{
  "module_name": "top_module",
  "io": [
    {"name": "clk", "dir": "input", "width": 1, "description": "Clock; state sampled on posedge"},
    {"name": "x", "dir": "input", "width": 1, "description": "Input selecting next state"},
    {"name": "y", "dir": "input", "width": 3, "description": "Present state"},
    {"name": "Y0", "dir": "output", "width": 1, "description": "Bit 0 of next state Y"},
    {"name": "z", "dir": "output", "width": 1, "description": "Moore output"}
  ],
  "clocking": {
    "clock": {"name": "clk", "edge": "posedge"},
    "reset": null
  },
  "timing": {
    "outputs": {
      "Y0": {"latency_cycles": 0},
      "z": {"latency_cycles": 0}
    }
  },
  "functional_summary": {
    "overview": "Moore FSM with 3-bit present state y and 1-bit input x. Outputs Y0 (LSB of next state Y) and z are combinational functions of y and x, sampled after posedge clk settles.",
    "rules": [
      "Y0 = 1 iff (y==3'b000 and x==1) or (y==3'b001 and x==1) or (y==3'b010 and x==1) or (y==3'b011 and x==0) or (y==3'b100 and x==0).",
      "Equivalently Y0 = (y[2]==0 and x==1) or (y==3'b011 and x==0) or (y==3'b100 and x==0).",
      "z = 1 iff y==3'b011 or y==3'b100; else z = 0.",
      "Next-state table: y=000 -> Y=000 (x=0) / 001 (x=1); y=001 -> 001 / 100; y=010 -> 010 / 001; y=011 -> 001 / 010; y=100 -> 011 / 100.",
      "Outputs are combinational (latency_cycles 0) and reflect inputs driven before the sampled posedge."
    ]
  }
}
